# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation Report

## Summary
Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for this Nuxt/Docus documentation project.

## Changes Made

### Created Files:
- **app.vue** - Root application file with Analytics component integration
  - Added `<script setup lang="ts">` section importing Analytics from '@vercel/analytics/nuxt'
  - Added `<Analytics />` component in the template
  - Wrapped content with `<NuxtLayout>` and `<NuxtPage />` to maintain Docus functionality

### Modified Files:
- **package-lock.json** - Updated after running `npm install` to ensure dependencies are properly locked

## Implementation Details

The `@vercel/analytics` package (v1.6.1) was already present in package.json but not configured. I created the app.vue file following Nuxt best practices:

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/nuxt';
</script>

<template>
  <div>
    <Analytics />
    <NuxtLayout>
      <NuxtPage />
    </NuxtLayout>
  </div>
</template>
```

This configuration:
- Imports the Analytics component specifically for Nuxt from '@vercel/analytics/nuxt'
- Places the component at the root level to track all page views
- Preserves the existing Docus theme structure using NuxtLayout and NuxtPage

## Testing Performed

1. ✅ **Dependencies installed** - Ran `npm install` successfully
2. ✅ **Build verification** - Ran `npm run build` - completed successfully without errors
3. ✅ **Dev server test** - Started dev server with `npm run dev` - runs without errors
4. ✅ **No linter configured** - Project doesn't have lint scripts in package.json
5. ✅ **No tests found** - Project doesn't have test files

## Notes

- The project uses Docus (a Nuxt documentation theme) with the `--extends docus` flag
- Analytics will automatically track page views when deployed to Vercel
- No additional configuration needed - the Analytics component works with zero-config on Vercel
- The implementation follows official Vercel documentation for Nuxt integration
